# Runtime state
/config.yaml
/data/
/_storage/
/_uploads/
/logs/
/certs/
/dist/
/.gotavern/

# Go build/test output
/gotavern
/gotavern.exe
/coverage.out
# Compiled test binaries. `go test` writes `<pkg>.test` (or `.test.exe` on Windows) into the package directory,
# and `go test -c` / a profiled run can leave one in the repository root. Untracked and unignored is the
# combination that makes a `git add -A` stage a binary (AGENTS.md rule 56: intent does not constrain the set).
*.test
*.test.exe
*.out
# CPU and heap profiles from the benchmarks in internal/server/bench_test.go.
/cpu.out
/mem.out
# The binaries the browser differential runs (`.browser-bin/gotavern` and `.browser-bin/mock-provider`,
# built by browser-differential.yml). It is ~70 MB of build output that lives in the working tree, and it
# was NOT ignored: a `git add -A` -- which this repository has already been burned by twice, once absorbing
# four other lanes' in-flight files -- would have staged it. Build output is not a source artefact.
/.browser-bin/

# Local reference build output
/upstream/generated/_webpack/

# Serialisation lock for concurrent pinned-probe boots (tools/pinned-boot-lock.mjs)
/.pinned-boot-lock/
oracle-rerecord.patch

# Phase 1 private differential fixtures. REAL user data lives OUTSIDE this repository and is referenced
# READ-ONLY; nothing under this path is ever committed, staged or printed in full. Only opaque results
# (categories, counts, field names) may leave it. See docs/local-preflight.md for the read-back rule.
/.private-fixtures/

# Local qualification scratch: private tree copies, downloaded CI artefacts and probe reports. Never committed,
# never uploaded, and never printed. The pin gate and the markdown walk both skip gitignored directories.
/.tmp-artifacts/
/tests/browser/.tmp-artifacts/
